# Git / GitHub Pages sync (taoshenn.cloud)

This site deploys from `main` on GitHub Pages.

## Do not upload / push unless asked

- **Never** `git push`, publish, or deploy to GitHub Pages unless the user **explicitly** asks (e.g.「上传」「推送」「部署」).
- Local edits and local commits are fine when the user asks to change the site; **stop before push**.
- Do not use the GitHub web UI to publish as a workaround unless the user asks to deploy.

## Single source of truth

- **Edit only in the local workspace**.
- **Do not** create or edit site files on github.com while local work exists, unless you immediately `git pull` afterward.
- Prefer: change locally → (commit if asked) → push **only if user asked to deploy**.

## Before every push (only when user requested deploy)

```powershell
cd d:\Web\taoshenn.cloud
git fetch origin
git pull
git push origin main
```

This repo uses `pull.rebase true` locally — keep it.

## If push is rejected (remote ahead)

1. `git pull` (rebase) — do **not** `git push --force` unless the user explicitly asks.
2. Resolve conflicts; for the live homepage prefer the **local** intended design unless the user says otherwise.
3. `git push origin main`.

## If rebase is stuck / messy

```powershell
git rebase --abort
git fetch origin
git reset --hard origin/main
# re-apply the intended file changes, commit once, then push only if asked
```

Never leave an interactive rebase half-finished across sessions.

## Network (China → GitHub)

If `git push` fails with connection timeouts, retry with a working network/proxy, or ask the user to push. Do not invent a second history by re-creating the repo on the web.
